cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PTMlink, please cite the preprint below and name the data release
  you used. The journal article's reference and the archive DOI are added to
  this file when they exist.
title: "PTMlink: a database resource for co-variation of glycosylation and phosphorylation in human tumors"
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
url: "https://ptmlink.biomarkercenter.org/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Effram360/PTMlink"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  PTMlink scores pairs of an N-linked glycosylation site and a phosphorylation
  site measured in the same tumors by their co-variation across twelve CPTAC
  tumor cohorts: a covariate-adjusted partial Spearman correlation within each
  cohort, combined across cohorts by fixed-effect meta-analysis, with each
  cohort's estimate, normal adjacent tissue where it was measured, annotations
  of shared protein abundance and tissue composition, and perturbation
  evidence from three studies that altered N-glycosylation in human cells.
keywords:
  - glycosylation
  - phosphorylation
  - post-translational modification
  - CPTAC
  - proteomics
  - co-variation
  - database
